  "title": "First FIFA World Cup (Uruguay 1930)",
  "summary": "The first FIFA World Cup was held in Uruguay from 13 to 30 July 1930, after a FIFA meeting in Amsterdam in 1928 and the push of president Jules Rimet. Thirteen teams entered and all games were played in Montevideo, though many European nations stayed away. In the final at the newly built Estadio Centenario, hosts Uruguay beat Argentina 4–2 to become the first winners. FIFA's congress had declared that the tournament would be arranged every four years.",
